WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:20.724
"Big Spot's saddle pad is missing?" Maggie said. "What do you mean?

2
00:00:20.725 --> 00:00:24.480
I put it back in the tack room, just like always!"

3
00:00:24.481 --> 00:00:28.273
"What's a tack room?" Cole whispered to Henry.

4
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:32.507
"I think it's where they keep the horses' equipment," he answered.

5
00:00:32.508 --> 00:00:36.337
"Are you sure?" Ms. Wood was asking Maggie.

6
00:00:36.338 --> 00:00:41.695
"Because the other pads were there. But yours wasn't with them."

7
00:00:41.696 --> 00:00:45.404
"I'm positive!" Maggie insisted.

8
00:00:45.405 --> 00:00:49.706
"I remember because it was kind of damp from Spot's sweat.

9
00:00:49.707 --> 00:00:54.591
I could feel it through my shirt when I carried everything back to the tack room."

10
00:00:54.592 --> 00:00:57.325
Ms. Wood didn't look convinced.

11
00:00:57.326 --> 00:01:00.825
"Well, I haven't seen it since your last lesson.

12
00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:06.576
If it doesn't turn up soon, I'll have to speak to your parents about replacing it."

13
00:01:06.577 --> 00:01:11.696
Henry looked at Cole, worried. Had the thief struck again?

14
00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:16.360
"I put a different pad under Spot's saddle," Ms. Wood went on.

15
00:01:16.361 --> 00:01:18.926
"You can use that one for today."

16
00:01:18.927 --> 00:01:24.731
The barn owner hurried away. Maggie stomped toward Big Spot's stall.

17
00:01:24.732 --> 00:01:27.070
The boys followed.

18
00:01:27.071 --> 00:01:30.765
"I can't believe this!" Maggie cried.

19
00:01:30.766 --> 00:01:34.686
"It's bad enough that my parents might not let me ride anymore.

20
00:01:34.687 --> 00:01:39.822
Now I have to worry about Ms. Wood kicking me out of the barn too!"

21
00:01:39.823 --> 00:01:44.092
"How much does a saddle pad cost?" Henry asked.

22
00:01:44.093 --> 00:01:47.706
"Why?" Maggie looked hopeful.

23
00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:52.944
"Are you going to buy Ms. Wood a new one so she doesn't tell my parents?"

24
00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:59.660
"No. I'm trying to figure out whether the thief could sell that pad for a lot of money."

25
00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:04.800
"Probably not." Maggie started changing into her riding boots.

26
00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:07.281
"The pad was kind of old.

27
00:02:07.282 --> 00:02:11.564
And saddle pads only cost about 15 dollars when they're new.

28
00:02:11.565 --> 00:02:16.043
I looked at some when Mom took me to the store to buy my riding clothes."

29
00:02:16.044 --> 00:02:19.846
"This case doesn't make sense," Cole said.

30
00:02:19.847 --> 00:02:23.508
"The thief is stealing really weird stuff."

31
00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:29.803
Henry nodded. "It's weird that only Maggie's stuff has disappeared.

32
00:02:29.804 --> 00:02:35.935
And it's even weirder that some of the missing stuff is valuable and some isn't."

33
00:02:35.936 --> 00:02:41.461
"A thief could sell Maggie's bracelet or her new riding gloves," Cole said.

34
00:02:41.462 --> 00:02:44.630
"And the check was worth money too, of course.

35
00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:50.229
But why steal one sock? Or a sweaty old saddle pad?"

36
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:54.324
"Who cares why someone did it?" Maggie said.

37
00:02:54.325 --> 00:02:59.237
"We just need to figure out who did it. And fast!"

38
00:02:59.238 --> 00:03:04.853
"Don't worry," Henry told her. "I have a plan, remember?"

39
00:03:04.854 --> 00:03:07.936
"Good. I hope it works."

40
00:03:07.937 --> 00:03:12.245
Maggie started getting her pony ready, and the boys wandered off.

41
00:03:12.246 --> 00:03:15.626
"Do you think your plan will work?" Cole asked.

42
00:03:15.627 --> 00:03:19.894
Henry stooped to pat Little Spot as the dog ran up to them.

43
00:03:19.895 --> 00:03:25.490
"I don't know. But it's the best plan I can think of right now."

44
00:03:25.491 --> 00:03:31.868
He was carrying a plastic bag. Reaching inside, he pulled out a baseball glove.

45
00:03:31.869 --> 00:03:37.406
"Are you sure you want to risk losing your autographed glove?" Cole asked.

46
00:03:37.407 --> 00:03:42.718
"It's really cool. Plus your parents will be mad if you lose it."

47
00:03:42.719 --> 00:03:49.005
"I won't lose it," Henry said. "We'll be hiding and watching it, remember?"

48
00:03:49.006 --> 00:03:51.169
That was his plan.

49
00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:56.106
The baseball glove had been autographed by several famous baseball players.

50
00:03:56.107 --> 00:03:59.123
Anyone could see it was worth a lot of money.

51
00:03:59.124 --> 00:04:04.507
Henry was planning to put the glove in the barn aisle where everyone would notice it.

52
00:04:04.508 --> 00:04:09.315
Then he and Cole would hide out and see if anyone tried to take it.

53
00:04:09.316 --> 00:04:14.071
With luck, they'd catch the thief before Maggie's riding lesson started!

54
00:04:14.072 --> 00:04:20.650
"If Jill is stealing because she needs money, she'll definitely grab this glove," Cole said.

55
00:04:20.651 --> 00:04:24.989
"If Zach's the thief, he might take it too," Henry said.

56
00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:30.766
"He loves baseball. And we don't know what Eleanor's motive might be.

57
00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:33.367
Maybe she needs money too.

58
00:04:33.368 --> 00:04:38.185
My aunt and uncle keep saying that riding is an expensive sport."

59
00:04:38.186 --> 00:04:44.718
He set his glove down. Then he and Cole hid in an empty stall nearby.

60
00:04:44.719 --> 00:04:47.997
It wasn't long before they heard footsteps.

61
00:04:47.998 --> 00:04:51.871
Henry peeked out and saw Zach coming down the aisle.

62
00:04:51.872 --> 00:04:58.124
"Hey, what's that?" Zach muttered. He stopped and picked up the glove.

63
00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:03.925
"Whoa, cool!" he said. "Guess someone will come back to look for this."

64
00:05:03.926 --> 00:05:09.161
He dropped the glove where he'd found it. Then he kept walking.

65
00:05:09.162 --> 00:05:14.309
"Zach didn't take the bait!" Cole whispered. "I guess he's innocent."

66
00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:20.989
Henry nodded. "Shh! Here comes Eleanor."

67
00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:29.727
Eleanor hurried down the aisle. "Spot? Spot, where are you?" she called.

68
00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:35.228
She was so busy calling her dog that she almost tripped over the glove before she saw it.

69
00:05:35.229 --> 00:05:38.220
Then she stopped, looking confused.

70
00:05:38.221 --> 00:05:41.464
She leaned down for a better look at the glove.

71
00:05:41.465 --> 00:05:46.135
Finally she shrugged and hurried off, still calling Spot.

72
00:05:46.136 --> 00:05:49.475
"Eleanor didn't take it either," Cole whispered.

73
00:05:49.476 --> 00:05:55.373
Henry just nodded. He'd heard the sound of Jill's wheelbarrow rolling toward them.

74
00:05:55.374 --> 00:06:00.881
The older girl saw the glove right away. She stopped her wheelbarrow.

75
00:06:00.882 --> 00:06:08.097
Then she hurried over, grabbed the glove, and took off down the aisle!
